    questionText: "A piggy bank contains only ₹5 coins and ₹2 coins, 25 coins in all, amounting to ₹95. Let the number of ₹5 coins be x and ₹2 coins be y. (i) Form the pair of equations. (ii) Solve by substitution. (iii) State how many coins of each type there are. (iv) Verify the total amount.",
    answer: "(i) x + y = 25 and 5x + 2y = 95. (ii) x = 15, y = 10. (iii) 15 five-rupee coins, 10 two-rupee coins. (iv) 5(15) + 2(10) = 75 + 20 = ₹95 ✓.",
